# which(1)

## NAME

which - locate a command

## SYNOPSIS

    which [-a] name...

## DESCRIPTION

Writes the path of the program for each name, searching `PATH` (or `/bin:/sbin`). Shell built-ins and functions are not searched; use `command -v` for those.

## OPTIONS

- `-a`: print every match

## EXIT STATUS

- `0`: every name was found
- `1`: a name was not found

## SEE ALSO

sh(1)
